From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juan Pablo Lassala <jpablolassala@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 04:42:20 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] main: Unset GDK_BACKEND under Camino

Camino, the Wayland compositor for MATE, starts mate-session as its child
with GDK_BACKEND=x11, because mate-session's dialogs call X11-only GDK
functions. mate-session hands its whole environment to every child, and
exports it to the D-Bus activation environment and to the systemd user
manager, so every MATE component would start on XWayland too.

Unset the variable right after gtk_init, when MATE_WM_NAME is Camino. Without
that, nothing changes.
---
 mate-session/main.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mate-session/main.c b/mate-session/main.c
index 68e3864..4b3ddae 100644
--- a/mate-session/main.c
+++ b/mate-session/main.c
@@ -642,6 +642,14 @@ int main(int argc, char** argv)
 		exit(1);
 	}
 
+	/* Camino starts mate-session with GDK_BACKEND=x11, since its dialogs need X11.
+	 * That is for this process only: its children, and the D-Bus and systemd
+	 * environments exported below, must not get it. */
+	if (g_strcmp0(g_getenv("MATE_WM_NAME"), "Camino") == 0)
+	{
+		g_unsetenv("GDK_BACKEND");
+	}
+
 	if (show_version)
 	{
 		g_print("%s %s\n", g_get_application_name(), VERSION);
